# Nothing under assets/ belongs in git. Track by EXCEPTION only.
#
# This used to list the raw pack's directories by name (/FBX/, /glTF/,
# /Textures/, ...), which worked exactly until someone unpacked a differently
# named pack next to them: "Modular Character Outfits - Fantasy[Source]" and
# "Universal Base Characters[Source]" matched none of those rules and 1.6 GB of
# raw art was staged for commit. An allowlist cannot fail that way.
#
# What lives here: raw art packs (hundreds of MB, several export formats each)
# and the pipeline outputs in generated/ that tools/build_medieval_assets.py
# rebuilds from them. The playground falls back to a procedural-only scene when
# generated/ is absent, so a fresh clone still builds and still passes smoke.
*
!.gitignore
